# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17203> (L-proline)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17203> "Pyrrolidine in which the <em>pro</em>-<i>S</i> hydrogen at position 2 is substituted by a carboxylic acid group. <small>L</small>-Proline is the only one of the twenty DNA-encoded amino acids which has a secondary amino group α to the carboxyl group. It is an essential component of collagen and is important for proper functioning of joints and tendons. It also helps maintain and strengthen heart muscles.")
