AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17823> "A hydroxycalciol that is calcidiol in which the <em>pro</em>-<i>S</i> hydrogen of calcidiol is replaced by a hydroxy group. It is the active form of vitamin D<small><sub>3</sub></small>, produced fom calciol <em>via</em> hydoxylation in the liver to form calcidiol, which is subsequently oxidised in the kidney to give calcitriol.")
